  <entry>
    <id>https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/pecan-and-ginger-flapjacks</id>
    <title>Pecan and ginger flapjacks</title>
    <updated>2026-06-20T16:10:13.043823+00:00</updated>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1 style="text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;"&gt;Pecan and ginger flapjacks&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;br&gt;
        &lt;img src="https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/pecan-and-ginger-flapjacks.webp" style="text-align:center;"/&gt;
        &lt;br&gt;
        &lt;p style="font-family:sans-serif;&gt;This batch of flapjacks have a deliciously sweet and buttery undertone of spice. The pecans give that butteriness, while the ginger biscuits almost completely dissolve into the mix, giving pops of caramelized ginger. They’re a great, cozy winter treat and will keep for a week in an airtight container.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <link href="https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/pecan-and-ginger-flapjacks"/>
